"""Manually authored curation; code only serializes researcher decisions."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,datetime
OUT=Path(__file__).parent
claims=[]; problems=[]; readings=[];links=[];coverage=[]
def C(n,scans,file,lines,words,statement,status,theme,computation='No numerical computation; symbolic argument or definition.',confidence='medium'):
    cote='156-'+str(n).split('-')[0]
    claims.append(dict(id='C-SA21-'+str(n),items=[],cote=cote,scans=scans,lines=[file+':'+lines],his_statement=words,statement=statement,status_on_pages=status,computation=computation,**{'class':'SEARCH_PENDING'},fate='',fate_date='2026-11-19',present_status='',refs=[],confidence=confidence,search_theme=theme))
def P(n,title,loc,his,today,why='The supplied text records a task or uncertainty; no external source documenting why it was left open has been found.'):
    problems.append(dict(id='MP-SA21-'+str(n),title=title,occurrences=loc,as_he_states=his,plausible_today=today,state_of_art='',why_open=why,worth='',refs=[]))
def R(cote,scan,line,reading,alternative,evidence,weight='high',confidence='medium'):
    readings.append(dict(cote=cote,scan=scan,line=line,reading=reading,alternative=alternative,evidence=evidence,weight=weight,confidence=confidence))
def L(kind,a,b,what,evidence,ids=''):
    links.append(dict(kind=kind,**{'from':a,'to':b},what=what,evidence=evidence,note_ids=ids))
def V(file,scans,note,comments):coverage.append(dict(folder=file,cote='156-'+file.split('-')[1],scans=scans,transcription_read='all lines',notes_read='all lines',claims_note=note,comments=comments))

# 156-8, folders 01–02, read completely 2026-11-19.
C('8-001',[3,8],'J156-8-01','12-87;237-266','Mag 1 ... Mag 4','A magasin is a set M with two partial orders ≤⊆≪ and a symmetric irreflexive relation ⟂°; for X≪Y the face set {Z≤Y:X≪Z} has a least element, denoted its carrier; X≪°Y means this carrier is Y. Interior disjointness is preserved by ≪° in both arguments; any two distinct faces of one element are interior-disjoint. The overview distinguishes local, faithful-shadow, point-like, set-theoretic, and moderate cases. This is an axiomatic definition, not a claim that arbitrary spaces satisfy it.','stated without proof','magasins')
C('8-002',[4,6],'J156-8-01','94-155;179-202','Les maquettes orienteuses de dim ≤1 sont les graphes','For the oriented-maquette axioms on scan 4, dimension ≤1 data reduce to vertices S, oriented edges A, a fixed-point-free involution a:A→A, and source σ:A→S; the target is σ∘a. This permits loops; an ordinary incidence poset cannot retain two endpoint incidences of a loop. The inverse equivalence presumes the stated signed-zero-cell convention.','proof sketched','graphs')
C('8-003',[6],'J156-8-01','204-204','Sauf erreur ... complexes cellulaires combinatoires de dim ≤2','Tentative assertion that oriented maquettes of dimension ≤2 describe combinatorial cell complexes. No precise category of complexes, attaching-map hypotheses, or equivalence functors are supplied; the strongest justified record is this proposed correspondence.','open on the pages','cellposets',confidence='low')
C('8-004',[9,12],'J156-8-01','292-340','figure ... fermé ... pour ≤ ... Sup ... union ... Inf ... intersection','For the magasin axioms, a figure is a ≤-lower subset whose elements are pairwise compatible. Nonempty intersections of figures are figures; a union is a figure exactly when its members are mutually compatible. Thus compatible joins are unions, nonempty meets are intersections, and the principal-ideal map X↦↓X embeds M. Refinement F≪G means each X∈F refines some Y∈G. Unconditional existence of the empty meet is not asserted.','proof sketched','order')
C('8-005',[10,11],'J156-8-02','20-71;104-110','Si X≷Y ... X |°| Y ⇔ X≠Y','In a magasin, compatibility is symmetric/reflexive and hereditary to faces. Compatible distinct elements are interior-disjoint. If X,Y are compatible and Z≪°X, then Z≪Y iff X≤Y; in particular, two compatible open carriers of Z coincide, and on compatible figures refinement equals inclusion. The text proves the elementary assertions and states the figure extension.','proved there','magasins')
C('8-006',[11],'J156-8-02','73-100','implique ... Mais on n’a pas nécessairement X≪°Y','Open refinement is transitive. If X≪Y≪Z and X≪°Z then Y≪°Z, but X≪°Y need not hold. The originally written equivalence is deleted and replaced by implication; an interval-with-interior-point picture illustrates failure of the other implication.','corrected by himself later (both places)','magasins')
C('8-007',[12,13],'J156-8-02','130-183','G′=Inf^≪(F′,G) ... commute aux Sup et aux Inf quelconques','For G≪F and F′≤F, the restriction G|F′ is the figure with underlying elements G∩Omb(F′), is the ≪-meet of G and F′, and defines a monotone map Sub(F)→Sub(G) preserving all joins and meets. If G≤F it is ordinary intersection. Quantification is within these principal subfigure lattices, where top and bottom exist.','stated without proof','sheaf')
C('8-008',[13,14],'J156-8-02','186-245','Recollement des raffinements ... exact','For compatible figures F,G with L=F∩G and refinements F′≪F,G′≪G, compatibility and disjointness are detected on F′|L,G′|L. For a cover F=⋃F_i, refinements glue uniquely from refinements of F_i agreeing on F_i∩F_j; equivalently Raff(F)=lim_{X∈F} Raff(X). Inclusion, compatibility, disjointness and refinement among refinements are local on the cover.','stated without proof','sheaf')
C('8-009',[15,16],'J156-8-02','277-339','Mog L 2 ... implique Mog L 1','Lieux are ≪-minimal elements. Interior shadows are omb°(X)={x lieu:x≪°X}. If X⊥°Y, every x∈omb°X is disjoint from every y∈omb°Y in the induced relation on lieux. The converse of THIS universal relational condition is the added axiom Mog L2; it is not merely disjointness of the two underlying sets unless distinct lieux are already disjoint. L2 implies nonempty interior shadows Mog L1 by irreflexivity (apply X=Y). The comment that practical examples satisfying L1 also satisfy L2 is explicitly tentative, not a theorem.','proof sketched','magasins')
C('8-010',[16,17],'J156-8-02','341-374','revient au même ... pré-ensemblistes','Assuming ≤⊆≪ with least carriers and nonempty interior shadows, a symmetric irreflexive disjointness relation on lieux, separating the interior shadows of distinct faces of a common element, determines a strictly divisible magma by universal disjointness on interior shadows. When distinct lieux are disjoint, the face-separation axiom follows from uniqueness of carriers; these are the pre-set-theoretic magmas. No embedding into figures of lieux is claimed: a counterexample is referred to on manuscript p.57.','proof sketched','magasins')
C('8-011',[15,17],'J156-8-02','317-324;378-386','Ssfig(F) ≃ Ssfig(mulomb(F))','Under Mog L1, taking multishadows preserves inclusion, refinement, compatible joins and meets, and disjointness; for each fixed figure F it induces an isomorphism of its subfigure poset with that of mulomb(F). This is a local-in-F claim and does not imply global faithfulness.','stated without proof','magasins')
P('8-01','Oriented maquettes and two-dimensional cell complexes',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':6,'file':'J156-8-01','lines':'204'}],'Sauf erreur, dimension ≤2 gives combinatorial cellular complexes.','Specify attaching data and multiplicities; compare signed incidence structures first for regular finite 2-complexes, then test loop edges and repeated incidences.')
P('8-02','Does local nonemptiness force local disjointness detection?',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':16,'file':'J156-8-02','lines':'330-339'}],'In practical cases Mog L1 seems to imply Mog L2.','L1 alone is weaker than L2; a meaningful result must specify a class of geometric magasins and prove that interior disjointness is detected on their lieux.')
P('8-03','Recover refinement from incidence and disjointness',[{'cote':'156-8','scan':14,'file':'J156-8-02','lines':'247-267'}],'Revisit lieux, shadows, supports and the case where ≪ is expressible in terms of ≤ and |°|.','Develop the support construction below and characterize exactly which magasins recover open refinement from support inclusion. This is revisited in later VIII, so the task is not automatically still open.')
R('156-8',4,'J156-8-01:119','X≪°Y′ ⇒ X⁻≪°Y⁻','Use Y on the left or Y′ on the right','The displayed implication changes the free variable; involution invariance must refer to the same Y.')
R('156-8',4,'J156-8-01:144','Z<X; codim(Y,X)=2','codim(Z,X)=2','Y is the intermediate object later quantified; the codimension-two condition belongs to Z.')
R('156-8',15,'J156-8-02:303','∂X={Y:Y≤X}','∂X={Y:Y<X}','The same line defines ∂X=↓X∖{X}; ≤ would include X and force every interior shadow empty.')
R('156-8',13,'J156-8-02:197','pour tout G≤G','pour tout G′≪G','The quantified variable is otherwise absent from the conclusion and the preceding proposition concerns refinements G′≪G. The ink must decide the missing prime/relation.')
V('J156-8-01','2–9','8-001–004','Scans 5 and 7 are recycled Récoltes et Semailles typescript, not geometric claims; scan 8 dated 26 June 1986.')
V('J156-8-02','10–17','8-005–011','Scan 10 dated 27 June; scan 17 continues into next folder.')

def save():
    claim_fields=['id','items','cote','scans','lines','his_statement','statement','status_on_pages','computation','class','fate','fate_date','present_status','refs','confidence']
    for name,data in [('claims',[{k:c[k] for k in claim_fields} for c in claims]),('problems',problems)]: (OUT/(name+'.json')).write_text(json.dumps(data,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
    for name,data,fields in [('readings',readings,['cote','scan','line','reading','alternative','evidence','weight','confidence']),('links',links,['kind','from','to','what','evidence','note_ids']),('coverage',coverage,['folder','cote','scans','transcription_read','notes_read','claims_note','comments'])]:
        with (OUT/(name+'.tsv')).open('w') as f:
            w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=fields,delimiter='\t');w.writeheader();w.writerows(data)
    print(json.dumps({'claims':len(claims),'problems':len(problems),'readings':len(readings),'folders_read':len(coverage)}))
if __name__=='__main__':
    for part in sorted(OUT.glob('curated_*.py')):
        exec(compile(part.read_text(),str(part),'exec'),globals())
    save()
